rs fifty five percent  estate tax when you get to fifty million  dollar estates and if people are passing  on estates bigger than a billion dollars  a 77 percent estate tax that would raise  thirty one and a half billion dollars we  could end fossil fuel subsidies that  would raise twenty six billion dollars  there's an accounting measure called  LIFO which means last in first out you  don't have to understand what it is but  that would eliminate that would raise  eleven  two billion and if we raised the  long-term capital gains rate from 15  percent to 20 percent that would raise  five billion dollars now you don't need  nearly all of this stuff this is the  really important thing I've given you  given you a list of a dozen or so ideas  for how you can raise money you might  not like some of that stuff so let's  just pick and choose one configuration  so now let's compare what these programs  would cost versus what we might save  Medicare for all tuition free public  college paid family paternal maternal  leave and the Social Security expansion  we're talking about one point four three  two trillion I'm only picking a few of  those ideas I mentioned to you what if  we eliminated the Bush and Trump tax  cuts did the employer and household tax  that I mentioned exempting of course the  first two million in payroll for  businesses and the first $29,000 in  income for families and raised the  social security cap to two hundred and  fifty thousand that would raise 1.5  trillion dollars you can disagree with  exactly how much money we would raise by  ending the Bush tax cuts maybe you don't  think it's I believe it was four hundred  and eighty eight billion maybe you think  it would only raise 450 for example you  can say you know I don't really want to  raise the social security cap at all  well then replace that with some of the  other ideas I presented but the point is  we have more than enough tools simple  tools to raise the money to cover what  these programs would